# SingletonColorRegistry

**File:** `src/yasched/utilizing/SingletonColorRegistry.py`

The process-wide singleton color registry. Combines `ColorRegistry` with
`GenericSingleton` so that exactly one instance exists per process, accessible
from anywhere via `get_instance()`.

`Color.from_name()` delegates its name lookup to this class.

---

## Interface

```
SingletonColorRegistry
  extends ColorRegistry
  extends GenericSingleton
  --
  (no new methods — inherits everything from ColorRegistry and GenericSingleton)
```

---

## Relationship to ColorRegistry

`ColorRegistry` is a reusable plain class. `SingletonColorRegistry` adds
nothing new beyond enforcing the singleton constraint. This separation allows:

- Unit tests to create isolated `ColorRegistry` instances without polluting
  the global singleton.
- Application code to use `SingletonColorRegistry.get_instance()` and always
  access the same shared registry.

---

## Notes

- CSS pre-loading (from `ColorRegistry.__init__`) runs once on first
  instantiation. Subsequent `get_instance()` calls return the same populated
  instance.
- `_reset_instance()` (inherited from `GenericSingleton`) clears the singleton
  for test teardown. It also loses all previously registered colors.
